@page "/loading-and-restoring"
@using CachingDemo.Client.Persistence
@using RevalQuery.Core.Abstractions.Query
@using RevalQuery.Core.Query.Options
@* No prerender. The persistence adapter is registered in the WebAssembly host only, so a
   prerender would fetch on the server and transfer the result, which is precisely the restore
   this page exists to show. *@
@rendermode @(new InteractiveWebAssemblyRenderMode(prerender: false))
@inherits RevalQuery.Blazor.QueryComponentBase

<PageTitle>Loading covers restores</PageTitle>

<h1>Loading covers restores</h1>

<p>
    A restore is a read from persistence, and it is not a fetch: <code>IsFetching</code> stays
    false throughout one. From 0.4.0 a query exposes <code>IsRestoring</code>, and
    <code>IsLoading</code> is <code>(IsFetching || IsRestoring) &amp;&amp; IsPending</code>, so a
    component that renders a spinner on <code>IsLoading</code> covers both waits.
</p>

<p>
    This page's store takes @SlowDemoPersistence.Delay.TotalSeconds seconds to answer. Reload
    the page to watch it again.
</p>

<h2>Seeded key, fresh enough to skip the fetch</h2>
<p>
    Something was stored under <code>("persisted", "profile")</code> before the page loaded, and
    its stale time has not passed, so the restore is the whole story. Nothing is fetched at all.
    Judged on <code>IsFetching</code> alone this query would look idle and empty, and the page
    would show its empty state for @SlowDemoPersistence.Delay.TotalSeconds seconds before the
    data appeared.
</p>
<StateTable State="Profile" />
<p>Data: <strong>@(Profile.Data ?? "none yet")</strong></p>

<h2>Empty key, restore then fetch</h2>
<p>
    Nothing is stored under <code>("persisted", "orders")</code>. The restore still has to run
    and come back empty before the query knows it must fetch, so this one is loading twice over:
    first restoring, then fetching.
</p>
<StateTable State="Orders" />
<p>Data: <strong>@(Orders.Data ?? "none yet")</strong></p>

@code {
    IQueryState<string> Profile => UseQuery(
        QueryOptions
            .Create<(string, string), string>(
                ("persisted", "profile"),
                async static ctx => await FetchAsync("profile", ctx.CancellationToken ?? default))
            .ConfigureFetch(fetch => fetch.StaleTime(TimeSpan.FromMinutes(5)))
            .Build());

    IQueryState<string> Orders => UseQuery(
        QueryOptions
            .Create<(string, string), string>(
                ("persisted", "orders"),
                async static ctx => await FetchAsync("orders", ctx.CancellationToken ?? default))
            .ConfigureFetch(fetch => fetch.StaleTime(TimeSpan.FromMinutes(5)))
            .Build());

    private static async Task<string> FetchAsync(string what, CancellationToken ct)
    {
        await Task.Delay(1500, ct);
        return $"{what} from the network at {DateTimeOffset.Now:HH:mm:ss}";
    }
}
